ai-dev-pipeline v7 helper: compiles pipelines into Workflow scripts and manages runs, the vault, tickets and flows

Usage: <BIN> [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  validate     Validate a pipeline YAML (schema + composition: refs, cycles, inputs)
  pipeline     Discover pipelines: `list` them, `show` one, or `expand` its compositions
  run          Run lifecycle: init, start, state, summary, reconcile, resume anchors
  scope        Scope checking
  agents       Discover registered agents
  skills       Resolve a skill name
  skill-rules  Check the stage diff against the rules of the loaded skills
  topo         Topo-sort a pipeline
  progress     Render run progress (markdown)
  gate         Gate lifecycle: approve/abort/pending. Persists the decision then hands back exactly what the driver needs to act on it
  gh           GitHub verbs (pull requests, checks, review threads, workflow runs) through the `gh` CLI
  project      Facts about a project directory (stack detection)
  mock         Run the local mock HTTP server
  workflow     v7 engine: compile a run into a Claude Code Workflow script
  vault        v7: the Obsidian vault that holds everything pipelines produce
  knowledge    v7: the per-project knowledge base — its two layers, and the create-or-update decision for a feature note
  gateway      The resident control plane: headless claude sessions, automations (cron / webhook / event), HTTP API + SSE for the viewer
  ticket       The local ticket backlog under `<vault>/TODO/`, only ever written by `<BIN>`: an agent must never hand-edit a ticket's status or frontmatter
  flow         Ticket flows: validate a definition, start and drive a run through the daemon
  rag          RAG over the project corpus: index and search BIBLE, docs, C# code, runs and tickets
  memory       Project memory: lessons and decisions injected into pipeline stages
  doctor       Self-check: binary, templates, agents, hooks, schemas, vault
  status       List runs found in the vault, and under `.aidp/pipelines/` in the current workspace
  setup        Setup helpers (cross-platform JSON merge for hooks, etc.)
  cost         Cost measurement: per-run breakdown, JSONL ledger, counterfactual and anomaly detection. Never changes a `model:` or makes a routing decision
  git          Git history as a differed signal: commit outcomes (revert, hotfix, success) derived from history, never from the reply envelope
  findings     Deterministic findings.json merge: fold N axis reviews into one canonical verdict mechanically instead of via a synthesis model
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace-root <PATH>
          Workspace to act on instead of the current directory

      --vault <PATH>
          Obsidian vault to use instead of `AIDP_VAULT`, `~/.aidp/config.json` or auto-detection

      --no-vault
          Ignore any vault and keep artefacts in the repo (`.aidp/pipelines/`)

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. Each command keeps its own default when omitted

          Possible values:
          - json-compact: One compact JSON document on a single line
          - json-pretty:  One indented JSON document
          - ndjson:       One compact JSON value per line
          - text:         Human-readable text
          - footer:       The one-line cost footer of a report, for `<BIN> cost ticket`; text elsewhere

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr; repeat for more (`-vv`)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes: 0 success, 1 internal, 2 hook wake, 3 not found, 4 policy refusal, 5 upstream failure, 6 negative verdict, 7 usage. See the "Exit codes" section of README.md.
